P.append(mcq(4,'Where an impact removes most rotation','A.4','ahl',r'A horizontal turntable has moment of inertia $I$ and initial angular speed $\omega$. Clay of mass $m$ is dropped vertically and sticks at radius $r$, with $mr^2=I$. In a separate identical trial it sticks at radius $r/2$. External torque about the axis is negligible. What is the ratio of rotational kinetic energy lost in the first trial to that lost in the second?', [r'$5/2$',r'$4$',r'$2$',r'$5/4$'],r'Conservation of angular momentum gives $\omega_f=I\omega/(I+mr^2)$ and $\Delta K/K_i=mr^2/(I+mr^2)$. The losses are $K_i/2$ and $K_i/5$, respectively. Their ratio is $5/2$, not $4$: the final angular speed also changes with radius.',C(7,3),'Off-axis sticking collision and rotational-energy loss','Uses two impact radii and a nonlinear energy-loss ratio rather than identifying a graph.','Combine angular-momentum conservation with dissipated rotational energy.',d))
