P.append(mcq(7,'Radiation into warm surroundings','B.1','core',r'A black surface of area $A$ at temperature $T$ radiates into surroundings at negligible temperature, with net power $P$. A second surface has area $2A$, temperature $2T$ and emissivity $0.25$. It is surrounded by a large enclosure at temperature $T$. What is its net outward radiative power? Assume absorptivity equals emissivity.', [r'$7.5P$',r'$8P$',r'$3.75P$',r'$0.5P$'],r'The first power is $P=\sigma AT^4$. The second net power is $\epsilon(2A)\sigma[(2T)^4-T^4]=0.25\times2\times15P=7.5P$. The $8P$ distractor neglects absorbed enclosure radiation; using the temperature difference to the fourth power is also incorrect.',C(10,4),'Area, emissivity and fourth-power radiative scaling','Adds finite-temperature surroundings and asks for net rather than emitted power.','Distinguish emission from net energy transfer before scaling.'))
