Q.append(written('2',1,'A cut pendulum and an uphill collision','A.2','core',r'A $0.300\,\mathrm{kg}$ pendulum bob on a light $1.25\,\mathrm m$ string is released from rest at $60.0^\circ$ to the downward vertical. At the lowest point the string is cut immediately before the bob collides horizontally with a stationary $0.450\,\mathrm{kg}$ trolley. The bob sticks to the trolley, and the combined mass moves onto a frictionless ramp. Air resistance and rolling losses are negligible. Take $g=9.81\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-2}}$.',[
 ('a',r'Calculate the bob’s speed immediately before the string is cut.',2),
 ('b',r'Calculate the string tension immediately before it is cut.',2),
 ('c',r'Determine the maximum vertical height reached by the combined bob and trolley, measured from the collision level.',3),
 ('d',r'Explain why horizontal momentum is conserved during the short collision although mechanical energy is not.',2),
 ('e',r'Calculate the fraction of the bob’s pre-collision kinetic energy dissipated in the collision.',1)], [
 ('a',[('M1',r'The vertical drop is $h=L(1-\cos60^\circ)=0.625\,\mathrm m$, and $mgh=\tfrac12mv^2$.'),('A1',r'$v=\sqrt{2(9.81)(0.625)}=3.50\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$.')]),
 ('b',[('M1',r'At the bottom, $T-mg=mv^2/L$; centripetal force is the resultant, not an additional force.'),('A1',r'$T=0.300[9.81+(3.5018)^2/1.25]=5.89\,\mathrm N$.')]),
 ('c',[('M1',r'Horizontal momentum gives $0.300v=(0.300+0.450)u$.'),('A1',r'$u=1.40\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$ after sticking.'),('A1',r'On the lossless ramp, $\tfrac12Mu^2=MgH$, so $H=u^2/(2g)=0.100\,\mathrm m$. Accept a consistent follow-through from part (a).')]),
 ('d',[('R1',r'The string has been cut and external horizontal impulse during the short collision is negligible; the bob–trolley system’s horizontal momentum is conserved.'),('R1',r'Sticking is inelastic: mechanical energy transfers to internal energy/deformation/sound. These transfers do not require loss of total energy.')]),
 ('e',[('A1',r'$K_f/K_i=m_\mathrm{bob}/(m_\mathrm{bob}+m_\mathrm{trolley})=0.400$, so the dissipated fraction is $0.600$.')])],('49.pdf',2,2),'Pendulum drop, bottom tension and a sticking collision','Uses a non-horizontal release and unequal trolley mass, cuts the string explicitly and separates collision/ramp energy budgets.','Track changing system boundaries and use the appropriate conservation law at each stage.',d,refs=['A.2','A.3']))
