Q.append(written('2',5,'Which ion reaches the end of the plates?','D.3','core',r'Horizontal plates of length $0.120\,\mathrm m$ are separated by $0.0400\,\mathrm m$ in a vacuum. Their potential difference is $320\,\mathrm V$, with the upper plate positive. A proton enters midway between them with horizontal velocity $3.00\times10^5\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}$. Edge fields and gravity are negligible. Use $e=1.60\times10^{-19}\,\mathrm C$ and $m_p=1.67\times10^{-27}\,\mathrm{kg}$.',[
 ('a',r'Calculate the electric field strength and the proton’s vertical acceleration, including directions.',2),
 ('b',r'Determine whether the proton reaches the far end of the plates. If it hits a plate first, determine the horizontal distance to impact.',3),
 ('c',r'An alpha particle, of charge $+2e$ and mass $4m_p$, enters at the same point and speed. Determine whether it hits a plate.',2),
 ('d',r'A uniform magnetic field is added so that either ion at the stated speed passes undeflected. Determine its magnitude and direction.',2),
 ('e',r'For an undeflected ion in the combined fields, state the net change in kinetic energy while it passes between the plates, with a reason.',1)], [
 ('a',[('A1',r'$E=V/s=320/0.0400=8.00\times10^3\,\mathrm{V\,m^{-1}}$, downwards from the positive plate.'),('A1',r'$a_p=eE/m_p=7.66\times10^{11}\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-2}}$, downwards.')]),
 ('b',[('M1',r'The nominal transit time is $L/v=4.00\times10^{-7}\,\mathrm s$; unbounded vertical deflection would be $\tfrac12a_pt^2=0.0613\,\mathrm m>0.0200\,\mathrm m$, so the lower plate is hit.'),('M1',r'Set $0.0200=\tfrac12a_pt_h^2$ to obtain $t_h=2.28\times10^{-7}\,\mathrm s$.'),('A1',r'$x_h=vt_h=0.0685\,\mathrm m$, less than $0.120\,\mathrm m$. The nominal-exit deflection is a test, not an actual path beyond impact.')]),
 ('c',[('M1',r'$a_\alpha=(2e)/(4m_p)\,E=a_p/2$. Its nominal-exit deflection is $0.0307\,\mathrm m$.'),('A1',r'This still exceeds $0.0200\,\mathrm m$, so the alpha also hits the lower plate, at $x=\sqrt2\,x_h\approx0.0969\,\mathrm m$.')]),
 ('d',[('A1',r'$qE=qvB$ gives $B=E/v=0.0267\,\mathrm T$, independent of ion charge-to-mass ratio.'),('R1',r'B must be into the page: for positive charge moving right, the magnetic force is then upward and opposes the downward electric force.')]),
 ('e',[('R1',r'The kinetic-energy change is zero. The net force vanishes, and the electric force is perpendicular to the straight trajectory; the magnetic force does no work.')])],('49.pdf',10,6),'Ion deflection between plates and crossed-field cancellation','Changes all geometric/field data so both ions impact, asks for impact positions and distinguishes nominal continuation from real motion.','Test the physical boundary before using an exit formula, then compare charge-to-mass effects.',d,refs=['D.3','D.2','A.1']))
