 ('b',[('M1',r'The positive loss of kinetic energy per unit mass equals $\overline g\,s$: $\overline g=(v_P^2-v_Q^2)/(2s)$. This defines the path average even though g is not constant.'),('A1',r'$\overline g=[7000^2-6800^2]/[2(3.00\times10^6)]=0.460\,\mathrm{N\,kg^{-1}}$ towards the planet.')]),
 ('c',[('M1',r'The mass defect is $3(4.00260)-12.00000=0.00780\,\mathrm u$; balanced electron counts permit use of the supplied atomic masses.'),('A1',r'$E=0.00780(931.5)=7.27\,\mathrm{MeV}$ per reaction.')]),
